GFOpenTorrent: the Preferences pages without Windows' headers.
- listeninterfacedialog: the adapter list from libtorrent's
  enum_net_interfaces (the TCP/IP stack's interfaces) through
  compat/gfot_netif.cpp, in place of GetAdaptersAddresses
- preferencesconnectionpage: no WinSock headers (none of it is used);
  a list item's text goes through ToStdString()
- preferencesdialog: the restart prompt is a wxMessageDialog with the
  same choice, in place of TaskDialogIndirect
- preferencesgeneralpage: no start-up list to join on AmigaOS (a program
  starts with Workbench when its icon is in SYS:WBStartup), so the "start
  with Windows" box is hidden and never set
- preferencesadvancedpage: MAKE_PROP no longer pastes a token onto '<'
  (GCC refuses it; Get<t3> is the same on every compiler)
Each AmigaOS change sits under __WXOPENLAYOUT__, Windows' code as it was.
